tweets.full_text:
@Tr0llyTr0llFace Very wrong.
1) the 8-K says OpenAI indemnifies NVDA for any amounts actually paid, so NVDA has recourse against the tenant.
2) Settlement requires a physical remarketing process of the data center. It's not a notional payment on a credit event. There's a building.

AIG failed on collateral calls against a notional many multiples of its equity, triggered by marks and a downgrade, with no recourse. NVDA's cap is under one year of net income, attaches per building from 2028, settles only after a re-let or sale, and carries an indemnity.
Reasoning by analogy is leading you to the wrong conclusion.

